# Electron Main Process Patterns

## BrowserWindow Configuration

Always use `getTitlebarOptions()` from the titlebar library instead of hardcoding frame/titlebar settings:

```typescript
// BAD -- hardcoded, not cross-platform
const mainWindow = new BrowserWindow({
  frame: false,
});

// GOOD -- platform-aware
import { getTitlebarOptions } from '@drycstud.io/electron-titlebar/config';
const mainWindow = new BrowserWindow({
  ...getTitlebarOptions(),
});
```

## IPC Handler Registration

Call `attachToWindow(ipcMain, mainWindow)` after the window is ready, not at creation time:

```typescript
// GOOD
mainWindow.on('ready-to-show', () => {
  attachToWindow(ipcMain, mainWindow);
  mainWindow.show();
});
```

## Platform Detection in Main Process

Use `process.platform` directly (not navigator/userAgent):

```typescript
const isMac = process.platform === 'darwin';    // macOS
const isWin = process.platform === 'win32';     // Windows
const isLinux = process.platform === 'linux';   // Linux
```

## Config Functions Must Run in Main Process

`setup()`, `getTitlebarOptions()`, and `attachToWindow()` use Node.js APIs (`process.platform`, Electron IPC). They are exported from the `config` entry point which runs in the main process. Never import them in renderer code.

## Preload Config

`preloadConfig()` runs in the preload script context. It uses `contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld` and must be called before the renderer loads.
